+# BLUE CURRENT V46.15.0 — OPERATOR CONSOLIDATION + USAGE EVIDENCE
+
+## Release scope
+
+V46.11–V46.15 begins actual operator consolidation without deleting working modules.
+
+### V46.11 — Merged Primary-Surface Summaries
+Primary operator surfaces can now aggregate mapped merge-source signals.
+
+Examples:
+- Reservation Operations can absorb Reservation Yield summaries.
+- Live Floor Operations can absorb Operational Digital Twin signals.
+- Kitchen Throughput can absorb Kitchen Operations / Predictive Service signals.
+- Labor Deployment can absorb Staff Operations / Workforce Intelligence.
+- Guest Recovery can absorb Service Recovery.
+- Shift Profit Pulse can absorb Margin Intelligence / Cost Variance.
+
+The consolidation layer uses existing AppState rather than creating duplicate backend services.
+
+### V46.12 — Role-Based Default Navigation
+Adds reversible default navigation models for:
+- Manager
+- Executive
+- Technical / platform operator
+
+Manager defaults remain the 12 primary shift surfaces.
+Executive defaults emphasize performance/profit/portfolio.
+Technical defaults emphasize platform/rationalization/runtime surfaces.
+
+Full Platform remains available as a fallback.
+
+### V46.13 — Duplicate Entry-Point Consolidation
+Navigation policy is now explicit:
+
+`merge-entry-points-into-primary-targets`
+
+The goal is to route operators through primary surfaces while retaining merged modules underneath until the consolidation is proven.
+
+### V46.14 — Operator-Use Evidence
+Adds non-destructive operator-use evidence captured in AppState when a consolidated surface is opened.
+
+Evidence records:
+- surface ID
+- action
+- active role
+- timestamp
+- source metadata
+
+No restaurant state is changed.
+
+### V46.15 — Evidence-Backed Deprecation Recommendations
+Deprecation candidates now receive evidence recommendations:
+- `evidence-needed`
+- `retain-until-more-evidence`
+- `retain-active-use`
+
+The governing policy is:
+
+`merge-before-delete-and-require-use-evidence`
+
+No module is automatically removed.
+
+## UI
+Adds the Operator Consolidation + Usage Evidence center with:
+- active role
+- role-default surface count
+- mapped primary merge count
+- recorded use evidence
+- deprecation-evidence count
+- role-default navigation controls
+- Full Platform restore
+- merged-source summaries
+- evidence-based deprecation review
+
+## Validation
+- `node scripts/maintenance/test-operator-consolidation.js` passed.
+- Manager default navigation validated at 12 surfaces.
+- Technical and Executive navigation defaults validated.
+- Reservation Operations correctly merged Reservation Yield summary evidence.
+- Operator-use evidence persisted in AppState.
+- A used deprecation candidate returned `retain-until-more-evidence`.
+- An unused deprecation candidate returned `evidence-needed`.
+- Duplicate HTML ID detected during validation was corrected rather than suppressing validation.
+- `npm run check` passed:
+  - 822 JavaScript files
+  - 704 client scripts
+  - 5,251 unique HTML IDs
+- Server startup passed as V46.15.0.
+- `/api/health` returned HTTP 200 with database connected and authentication enabled.
+- Authoritative runtime database SHA-256 remained unchanged.
+
+## Safety / fine-comb policy
+- No working module was deleted.
+- No live-execution behavior changed.
+- Navigation changes are reversible.
+- Usage evidence is operational UX evidence only; it does not mutate restaurant operations.
+- Runtime database is not included in this patch.
+
+## Next fine-comb milestone
+The next wave should convert the evidence model into a real consolidation scorecard:
+- duplicate navigation count
+- clicks-to-action
+- primary-surface coverage
+- role-specific task completion
+- unresolved handoff count
+- surface-use evidence by role
+- first evidence-backed deprecation shortlist
+
+Permanent removal should occur only when workflow coverage and operator evidence demonstrate that the capability is redundant.
